From 8f395a335316a9de99a668416dd9c7d81e7ff40f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Udhayveer Singh <udhayveersingh@Udhayveer.local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 01:50:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the darwin TUN framing that killed nativetun on its first
 packet

macOS utun prefixes every packet with a 4-byte address family, so
wireguard-go's darwin device reads at bufs[0][offset-4:] and refuses a
write with offset under 4. NetstackAdapter passes offset 0, which is
right on Linux and Windows and panics here with "slice bounds out of
range [-4:]": the tunnel came up, connected to MASQUE, and died on the
first packet off the device.

DarwinTunAdapter keeps the 4 bytes of headroom and hands MaintainTunnel
the bare IP packet, with a pooled scratch buffer so a per-packet
allocation does not land in the gaming path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
